+
+## Local appraisal artifacts
+
+The appraisal track can read canonical `<folio>.zip` artifacts from either a
+flat directory or a sharded tree such as
+`/workspace/downloads/broward/full-ingestion/artifacts/<shard>/<folio>.zip`.
+Supplying `--appraisal-local-dir` leaves the existing S3 bucket/prefix path
+unchanged and avoids AWS reads for the appraisal track.
+
+Use the bounded dry-run stage to validate the 50-artifact Broward pilot without
+`DATABASE_URL` or AWS credentials:
+
+```bash
+npm run load:bulk -- \
+  --tracks appraisal \
+  --jurisdiction-key broward_appraiser \
+  --appraisal-local-dir /workspace/downloads/broward/appraisal-validation-50 \
+  --dry-run \
+  --limit 50 \
+  --batch-size 50 \
+  --stage-dir .loader-runs/broward-pilot
+```
+
+The report reconciles artifacts, `properties`, parcels, distinct folios, and
+row-level source metadata. Batch CSVs are deleted after serialization, and the
+checkpoint in `--stage-dir` makes reruns skip completed artifacts. Use separate
+`--dry-run-checkpoint` and `--dry-run-report` paths when multiple validations
+share a stage directory.
+
+When a database is intentionally available, omit `--dry-run` to run the same
+local source through the existing resumable batch COPY/merge path. A positive
+`--batch-size` bounds staging disk usage to one batch. This repository does not
+load or publish data merely by configuring the local source.
